== Notes ==
* When Death uses The Hourglass, {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}'s tear is slow to respond and has a higher maximum speed, becoming difficult to control.

== Trivia ==
* Death appeared in the original ''The Binding of Isaac.''
* {{e|Conquest}} is the alternate version of him.
* Death is one of the [[wikipedia:Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse|Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse]].
* Death's scythe attack is a homage to [[wikipedia:Castlevania|Castlevania]]'s recurring boss, Death. Both summon four scythes that stay put for a few seconds, then home in on the player.
* Death's horse shares a visual similarity to a scythe, with the head's shape mimicking that of the tool's curved blade. 
* {{dlc|nr}} Death is currently the only enemy in-game that can use a status effect against Isaac.
* {{dlc|r}} Death is redrawn to resemble his sprite from the Flash ''Binding of Isaac'', which, in turn, resembles the "planet face" of Chapter 6: The End in ''Super Meat Boy'', another game by Edmund McMillen.
** The redraw also makes the visual similarity of Death's horse to a scythe more apparent. However the changed texture of the handle now no longer matches those of the summoned Death Scythes. 

